## 4. `include/strata/artifact/gguf_split.hpp` — `gguf_split_paths` silently accepts non-numeric shard numbers

**Responsibilities.** The function parses `-NNNNN-of-MMMMM.gguf` by checking each character is a digit, but if the check fails it returns `{any}` (single-shard fallback) rather than reporting a malformed name. A file named `model-abcde-of-00002.gguf` would be treated as a single-shard model, and the real shard 2 would never be opened.

**Change.** Distinguish "not a split name at all" (no `-of-` tag) from "malformed split name" (tag present but digits invalid) and throw on the latter.

```diff
--- a/include/strata/artifact/gguf_split.hpp
+++ b/include/strata/artifact/gguf_split.hpp
@@ -28,10 +28,14 @@
     int no = 0, n = 0;
     for (size_t i = 0; i < 5; ++i) {
         const char a = any[at - 5 + i], b = any[at + 4 + i];
-        if (a < '0' || a > '9' || b < '0' || b > '9') return {any};
+        if (a < '0' || a > '9' || b < '0' || b > '9')
+            throw std::runtime_error("malformed split shard name (non-digit in shard number): " + any);
         no = no * 10 + (a - '0');
         n = n * 10 + (b - '0');
     }
-    if (n < 1 || no < 1 || no > n) return {any};
+    if (n < 1 || no < 1 || no > n)
+        throw std::runtime_error("malformed split shard name (shard " + std::to_string(no) +
+                                 " of " + std::to_string(n) + "): " + any);
```

**Verification.**
1. `gguf_split_test` adds a case: a file named `test-abcde-of-00002.gguf` throws with "non-digit" in the message.
2. A file named `test-00003-of-00002.gguf` (shard 3 of 2) throws with "shard 3 of 2" in the message.
3. A file with no `-of-` tag still returns `{any}` without throwing.

