## 9. `include/strata/core/device.hpp` — `DeviceArena::alloc` has no overflow check on `used_ + bytes`

**Responsibilities.** `DeviceArena::alloc(bytes, align)` bumps `used_` by the aligned size. If `bytes` is near `UINT64_MAX`, `used_ + bytes` overflows and the bounds check `used_ + bytes > capacity_` passes, returning a pointer past the allocation.

**Change.** Add an explicit overflow guard.

```diff
--- a/include/strata/core/device.hpp
+++ b/include/strata/core/device.hpp
@@ -52,6 +52,8 @@
     // `align` must be a power of two; 256 keeps every sub-allocation at a sector boundary.
     void* alloc(uint64_t bytes, uint64_t align = 256);
```

